window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["17"]={"https://theconversation.com/canada-wants-to-rebuild-its-manufacturing-sector-but-its-losing-the-immigrant-workers-it-needs-295833":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"adc99d40444f9943f1c8ebb30ca32d0a30c91c36b3ca42ef1e93fdf89003a736","read":"https://theconversation.com/canada-wants-to-rebuild-its-manufacturing-sector-but-its-losing-the-immigrant-workers-it-needs-295833","bytes":192602,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Canada wants to rebuild its manufacturing sector, but it’s losing the immigrant workers it needs","by":[{"n":"Marshia Akbar","r":"Research Lead on Labour Migration and Director of the BMO Newcomer Workforce Integration Lab. Global Migration Institute, Toronto Metropolitan University"},{"n":"Devaanshi Khanzode","r":"Quantitative Researcher, Global Migration Institute, Toronto Metropolitan University"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T17:03:38Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The trade war with the United States has put manufacturing at the centre of Canada’s economic agenda by exposing its dependence on a single trading partner."]},{"k":"p","s":["U.S. tariffs on Canadian steel, aluminum, automobiles and other products ",["have disrupted cross-border supply chains","https://www.bankofcanada.ca/publications/mpr/mpr-2026-04-29/in-focus-2/"],", reduced exports in key industries and increased costs for manufacturers, while leaving businesses uncertain about future trade conditions."]},{"k":"p","s":["In response, the federal government is trying to strengthen Canada’s domestic industrial capacity and reduce its reliance on the American market."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Tariffs are reshaping Canadian manufacturing, but not all workers are being impacted the same way","https://theconversation.com/tariffs-are-reshaping-canadian-manufacturing-but-not-all-workers-are-being-impacted-the-same-way-274269"]]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["Buy Canadian policy","https://www.canada.ca/en/public-services-procurement/news/2025/12/buy-canadian.html"]," now prioritizes Canadian suppliers and domestic materials in federal procurement, while Ottawa’s ",["Defence Industrial Strategy","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/news-releases/2026/02/17/prime-minister-carney-launches-canadas-first-defence-industrial?hl=en-CA"]," aims to create 125,000 jobs by expanding domestic defence production. Prime Minister Mark Carney has also pledged to ",["double non-U.S. exports","https://unb.com.bd/category/Business/carney-vows-to-double-canadas-non-us-exports-says-country-cant-rely-on-one-partner/171237"]," within a decade."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, these initiatives say little about the people who will do the work. Canada’s industrial ambitions depend on having a skilled and available workforce, yet the tariff shock is affecting who works in Canadian factories."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our analysis of ",["Statistics Canada’s Labour Force Survey","https://www23.statcan.gc.ca/imdb/p2SV.pl?Function=getSurvey&SDDS=3701"]," suggests immigrant workers are bearing a disproportionate share of the employment losses."]},{"k":"h","s":["A recomposition of the factory floor"]},{"k":"p","s":["Manufacturing employment fell by only about three per cent between January 2025 and April 2026. But Statistics Canada’s Labour Force Survey shows a more substantial change in who holds those jobs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monthly estimates for smaller population groups can fluctuate considerably, but the pattern points to a growing disadvantage for immigrant workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Immigrants’ share of manufacturing employment slipped from just over 30 per cent to under 28 per cent by December 2025, and has recovered only slightly since."]},{"k":"p","s":["The losses have come in waves. In 2025, immigrant workers accounted for a growing share of manufacturing job losses, before Canadian-born workers also began experiencing more layoffs as trade pressures persisted. By April 2026, immigrants remained disproportionately affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nearly two-thirds of unemployed immigrants who had previously worked in manufacturing reported losing their jobs, compared with fewer than half of their Canadian-born counterparts, even as job loss became a less common reason for unemployment across the sector."]},{"k":"p","s":["These losses also appear more permanent. More than half of unemployed immigrant manufacturing workers reported a permanent layoff in April 2026, compared with about 43 per cent of Canadian-born workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["This coincided with ",["the April 2026 decision","https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/04/strengthening-actions-taken-to-adjust-imports-of-aluminum-steel-and-copper-into-the-united-states/"]," in the U.S. to extend steel, aluminum and copper tariffs to the full customs value of covered products, including certain derivative goods, rather than just their metal content."]},{"k":"h","s":["The skills Canada risks losing"]},{"k":"p","s":["Immigrant manufacturing workers are twice as likely as Canadian-born workers to hold a university degree — close to 40 per cent, compared with 20 per cent. This partly reflects Canada’s immigration system, which ",["awards significant points for education","https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/immigrate-canada/express-entry/check-score/crs-criteria.html"]," when selecting economic immigrants."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet higher education has not translated into better employment outcomes. Immigrant manufacturing workers earned nearly $3 an hour less than Canadian-born workers in April 2026, a gap that has widened since late 2025."]},{"k":"p","s":["One reason is that immigrants’ credentials are often discounted. Nationally, ",["more than one-quarter","https://theconversation.com/canadian-immigrants-are-overqualified-and-underemployed-reforms-must-address-this-247974"]," of university-educated immigrants work in jobs requiring no more than a high school education, more than double the rate for Canadian-born graduates."]},{"k":"p","s":["In manufacturing, immigrant workers hold far more degrees than their Canadian-born co-workers, yet earn less, suggesting many are working below their qualifications. Those roles, with ",["shorter tenure and lower pay","https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/pub/45-28-0001/2020001/article/00070-eng.htm"],", are also more exposed to layoffs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada will need engineers, technicians and quality specialists as it expands defence production, shipbuilding and advanced manufacturing. Many immigrants with these skills are already here, but are not working in their fields."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Ontario, internationally educated engineering graduates outnumber those with Canadian engineering degrees, yet ",["only 18 per cent work as engineers","https://ospe.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Census-Article-ALL-July2024-Final.pdf"],", compared with 40 per cent of Canadian graduates. Recognizing these credentials could be the fastest way to fill the skills gaps an expanding sector will face."]},{"k":"h","s":["The disadvantages facing immigrant women"]},{"k":"p","s":["The employment changes are also gendered. Women make up about one-third of immigrant manufacturing workers, compared with just over one-quarter of Canadian-born workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["When tariffs landed in spring 2025, women’s share of employment among immigrant manufacturing workers fell by two percentage points, while the share among Canadian-born workers barely moved."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the first eight months of 2025, immigrant women’s share of the overall manufacturing workforce shrank while Canadian-born women’s grew. ",["Caregiving responsibilities","https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/2022/12/supporting-gender-equality-by-addressing-barriers-to-employment.html"],", ",["language requirements","https://uwaterloo.ca/women-work-and-the-economy/sites/default/files/uploads/documents/advancing-equity-and-inclusion-strategies-for-integrating-racialized-immigrant-women-into-canadas-labour-market-by-marika-jeziorek.pdf"]," and ",["difficulties getting foreign credentials recognized","https://uwaterloo.ca/women-work-and-the-economy/sites/default/files/uploads/documents/labour-market-barriers-faced-by-highly-educated-racialized-newcomer-women-in-canada-by-ana-ferrer-and-sumeet-singh-dhatt.pdf"]," can make it more difficult for them to return to work after a layoff."]},{"k":"p","s":["Defence and advanced manufacturing are among the most male-dominated parts of the sector. Women are manufacturing’s largest untapped talent pool, and industry groups have long argued that ",["recruiting more women","https://www.plant.ca/features/hire-more-women-a-solution-to-the-skills-shortages-challenge/"]," is key to easing chronic skills shortages in manufacturing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Losing immigrant women already in the workforce further shrinks that talent pool, making it harder to fill the jobs Canada’s expanding industrial sector will create."]},{"k":"h","s":["Policies pulling in opposite directions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Federal policy has not adequately addressed the vulnerabilities immigrant workers face. In August, Ottawa announced a ",["$7.5-billion tariff-response package","https://www.canada.ca/en/department-finance/news/2026/08/support-for-canadian-workers-and-businesses-affected-by-us-tariffs.html"]," to support businesses and workers affected by U.S. tariffs. It includes additional income support, workplace training and a new Workforce Retention and Retraining Program. But these initiatives do not specifically address the employment barriers facing immigrants."]},{"k":"p","s":["The same month, Ottawa launched the ",["Advanced Manufacturing Workforce Alliance","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/news/2026/08/the-government-of-canada-announces-the-launch-of-the-advanced-manufacturing-workforce-alliance.html"],", one of six sector alliances designed to map skills gaps, align training with industry needs and help firms adopt new technologies. It brings together manufacturers, unions and training institutions."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the launch announcement makes no mention of immigrant workers or credential recognition, referring only broadly to underrepresented groups. Identifying the skills of immigrants already in the sector could help move them into the roles an expanding industry will need."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, some services immigrants rely on to enter and navigate the labour market are shrinking. Settlement funding outside Québec is expected to decrease by about ",["$98 million in 2026-27","https://www.ctvnews.ca/kitchener/article/newcomer-agencies-in-waterloo-region-brace-for-service-cuts-after-federal-funding-reduction/"],", and advanced language training is being ",["phased out","https://search.open.canada.ca/qpnotes/record/cic%2CIRCC-2025-QP-00014"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["These reductions could make it harder for newcomers to develop the language skills, professional connections and other supports needed to find suitable employment."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Buy Canadian framework sets out no workforce provisions. Canada is pledging to build more at home while weakening the systems that help skilled newcomers move into the jobs that effort requires."]},{"k":"h","s":["Building a better industrial strategy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada has good reason to diversify its markets and strengthen domestic production as manufacturers continue to navigate uncertainty with their largest trading partner."]},{"k":"p","s":["Trade tensions with the U.S. are likely to remain a defining challenge for Canadian manufacturing. The ",["July review of the Canada-United States-Mexico Agreement","https://www.canada.ca/en/global-affairs/news/2026/07/statement-by-minister-leblanc-following-trilateral-cusma-joint-review-meeting.html"]," ended without a deal to extend the pact, though it remains in force until 2036."]},{"k":"p","s":["Expanding domestic production, however, requires workers with the skills to sustain it. An industrial strategy must therefore make workforce retention a priority."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada cannot strengthen its manufacturing sector while overlooking the immigrant workers already contributing to it or failing to recognize the skills of those who could contribute more. If Canada wants to make more of what it needs at home, it must stop losing the skilled people it has already recruited to make it."]}],"chars":8079},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/denmark":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"12becc26e2a3971346ac9439b30a6e2bf5704ddcb5e86dce079eb687b3fd6618","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/denmark","bytes":78725,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Denmark travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-18T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:18:28+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice also covers the Faroe Islands and Greenland."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/denmark/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Denmark set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Danish Embassy in the UK","https://storbritannien.um.dk/en/about-us"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Denmark follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Denmark, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Denmark","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-denmark-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Danish border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay – the amount varies depending on your accommodation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must ",["meet the Danish government’s entry requirements","https://www.nyidanmark.dk/en-GB/You-want-to-apply"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you stay in Denmark with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Denmark","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-denmark#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["ID for travel from Denmark to Sweden"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling from Denmark to Sweden, see ",["information on border control requirements","https://www.oresunddirekt.se/en/find-a-job-in-denmark/commute-from-sweden-to-denmark/border-control-when-entering-sweden"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visas for Greenland and the Faroe Islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greenland and the Faroe Islands are not members of the EU. You do not need a visa to enter for tourism. If you plan to live and work there, you must get a work and residence permit – ",["apply for residence in Greenland or the Faroe Islands","https://www.nyidanmark.dk/en-GB/You-want-to-apply/The-Faroe-Islands-and-Greenland"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Delays at passport control"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the introduction of EES, you may experience delays at passport control when arriving at or departing from Copenhagen Airport on flights to or from non-Schengen countries, including the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should allow extra time when travelling through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a short onward connection, you should take this into account when planning your journey."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need assistance, for example if you are travelling with young children or have accessibility requirements, speak to airport staff wearing yellow vests who are managing the queues."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border controls at Germany’s land borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are temporary border controls in place to travel into Germany. Check the ",["entry requirements for Germany","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["TravelHealthPro’s Denmark guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/64/denmark#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["TravelHealthPro’s Faroe Islands guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/78/denmark-faroe-islands#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["TravelHealthPro’s Greenland guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/92/greenland#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Denmark","https://toldst.dk/en-us/individuals/special-rules-for-special-items"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import whale products from Greenland or the Faroe Islands into the UK or EU. You could be fined up to £5,000 or given a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Denmark"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Denmark"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is ",["10,000 euros or more","https://toldst.dk/en-us/individuals/travel/if-you-are-travelling-with-large-amounts-of-valuables"],". You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Denmark"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Denmark cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreigners."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are generally low, but pickpockets and bag-snatchers operate in crowded areas, mainly in Copenhagen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thieves use a variety of methods to distract you, particularly on crowded public transport. They sometimes also operate in hotel lobbies, cafes and restaurants."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your personal belongings, including passports and money, safe. Keep an eye on luggage, including in the overhead baggage compartment, when travelling on trains to and from the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpocketing and bag-snatching are common in the following areas of Copenhagen:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the central station"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nørreport Station"]},{"k":"li","s":["the main shopping street, Strøget"]},{"k":"li","s":["other areas popular with tourists such as Christiania, Nyhavn and Kongens Nytorv"]},{"k":"li","s":["inside Copenhagen Kastrup Airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care in Christiania and Nørrebro, particularly late at night. There have been some instances of gang violence in these areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to wear clothing that conceals your face in a public place in Denmark. There are legal exemptions – for example, face masks for health reasons. If you cover your face in public, you may get a fine of 1,000 krone (around £115). If you do it again, the fine can increase."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, are strictly prohibited, even in small quantities. Severe penalties apply for possessing, using, or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect long jail sentences of up to 10 years and substantial heavy fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Denmark have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships and marriage are legal in Denmark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Denmark, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Denmark guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/denmark/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Denmark. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience and a higher minimum age."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cyclists often have the right of way. Always check cycle lanes before turning right. Pedestrians also often have right of way to cross ahead of you if you are turning at traffic lights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-symbols-and-identifiers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Denmark, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bicycles and scooters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many bicycle accidents happen when pedestrians do not give the right of way to bicycles. There are online guides in English on cycling in Denmark at ",["Visit Copenhagen","https://www.visitcopenhagen.com/biking"]," and the ",["Danish Cyclists’ Federation","https://www.cyklistforbundet.dk/english/"]," (’Cyklistforbundet’)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Electric scooters are subject to road traffic rules. If you hire and use a scooter under the influence of alcohol, you could be prosecuted for drink-driving and you may be fined."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Arctic travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Greenland is in the Arctic Circle, and most of it is very remote. Emergency medical assistance and search and rescue services are limited in these areas. See ",["Arctic travel safety advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/arctic-travel-safety-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Greenland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel between towns is by air, sea or dogsled only. Arctic weather can affect travel, and you should be prepared for delays and cancellations."]},{"k":"p","s":["During busy periods or when there is travel disruption, there may be no accommodation available unless you have booked ahead."]},{"k":"p","s":["Supply chains are limited and travel times are long. Make sure you travel with sufficient prescription medication for all of your time in Greenland."]},{"k":"hs","s":["The Faroe Islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["Smaller roads may be unpaved and winding."]},{"k":"p","s":["The weather can change quickly, and you should prepare appropriately for the activity you are planning."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest vaccinations recommendations for ",["Denmark","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/64/denmark#Vaccine_Recommendations"],", ",["Greenland","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/92/greenland#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," and ",["the Faroe Islands","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/78/denmark-faroe-islands#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what other health risks you’ll face in ",["Denmark","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/64/denmark"],", ",["Greenland","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/92/greenland"]," and ",["Faroe Islands","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/78/denmark-faroe-islands"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Greenland. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Denmark does not recognise UK prescriptions. If you need medication, you should speak to a local pharmacist (‘Apotek’), who will be able to tell you if you need a prescription from a local GP."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Denmark"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Denmark","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/denmark-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards in Denmark"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Denmark, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Denmark","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-denmark"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards in Greenland"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will not be refused treatment, but an EHIC or GHIC will not cover the costs unless you are resident of a Nordic country, under the reciprocal agreement, or a resident of Denmark. You can find more details about ",["medical assistance available during a temporary stay in Greenland","https://www.norden.org/en/info-norden/medical-assistance-during-temporary-stay-greenland"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also have to cover the cost of medical evacuation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards in Faroe Islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot use a GHIC or EHIC in the Faroe Islands. The UK has reciprocal agreements with the Faroe Islands, so British nationals can get the same medical treatment they would with a GHIC or EHIC. This arrangement is not a substitute for travel insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to the Faroe Islands, you should still take your GHIC or EHIC with you. You’ll need to provide proof of identity and nationality, such as your UK passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Denmark"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Denmark"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Denmark"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Denmark"]," in Denmark"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Denmark","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/denmark-bereavement-packinformation/denmark-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Denmark","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/denmark-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/denmark/british-embassy-copenhagen"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/denmark/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Denmark","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-denmark"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":17385,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"08798464fe618f7c2970a33e88a82b35cfcdfe2798e4dfc1c25597ab2b3222eb","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea","bytes":57583,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Eritrea travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-30T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-09T16:20:13+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against FCDO advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 25km of all of Eritrea’s land borders."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the rest of Eritrea."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tensions between Eritrea and Ethiopia are high. If a crisis develops in Eritrea, the situation could change quickly, including your ability to travel within Eritrea or leave the country. Practical support from the British government such as face-to-face consular support or evacuation may be severely limited in a crisis. Read our ",["general guidance on consular support in a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be prepared to re-arrange your own departure from Eritrea if a crisis develops. If it is not safe or possible to leave, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay indoors whenever possible, and have a stock of essential supplies such as food, drinking water and medicine"]},{"k":"li","s":["obey any local restrictions such as curfews"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor the media for developments that would allow you to leave safely"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support for British nationals in Eritrea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Consular support is severely limited in parts of Eritrea. Staff at the British Embassy in Asmara cannot offer support in person in areas of Eritrea where FCDO advises against travel. Diplomats at the British Embassy require travel permits from the Eritrean government to travel outside Asmara, which means the Embassy cannot always provide consular assistance in person in parts of Eritrea."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Eritrean authorities may not inform the British Embassy if a British national is in need of help. There have been instances where the Eritrean authorities have refused to give the Embassy consular access to detained foreign nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Eritrea and you need urgent help (for example, you’ve been attacked or arrested, or someone has died), get in touch using the below:"]},{"k":"li","s":["during office hours, visit the British Embassy in Asmara at 66-68 Mariam Ghimbi Street. Office hours are Monday-Thursday between 8am and 4:30pm or Friday between 8am and 12:30pm"]},{"k":"li","s":["for out of hours support, call the British Embassy Addis Ababa on +251 116 170 100 or the Foreign Office in London on +44 207 008 5000"]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Eritrean dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British-Eritrean dual national or are of Eritrean origin, the Eritrean authorities consider you to be an Eritrean national. You may therefore be subject to obligations including taxes and national service. This may apply if you hold identity documents issued by Eritrea’s Department of Immigration and Nationality, including out of date documents, or if you do not hold these documents but are of Eritrean origin. The British Embassy is unable to offer consular assistance to dual nationals in Eritrea."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This advice reflects the UK government’s understanding of current rules for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK, for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Eritrea set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Eritrean Embassy in the UK","https://www.eritreanembassyuk.org.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Eritrea, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least 2 blank consecutive pages for stamping."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],".)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Eritrean dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dual nationals who enter Eritrea on an Eritrean identity card will need an exit permit from the Immigration Office in Asmara to leave the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Eritrea. For information about visas, contact the ",["Eritrean Embassy in the UK","https://www.eritreanembassyuk.org.uk/"]," or the nearest Eritrean embassy. Check with your airline or travel company for the latest information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccination requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip, check the ",["vaccinations and certificates you need in TravelHealthPro’s Eritrea guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/74/eritrea#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Depending on your circumstances, this may include a yellow fever vaccination certificate."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Eritrea. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electronic items"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare all laptops, mobile phones, cameras and other electronic items. If you do not, they can be confiscated by customs officials when you leave."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of Eritrea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare foreign cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 US dollars or more. You will get a certificate, which you must keep to show when you leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["When you leave Eritrea, you must be able to show that any foreign currency you have spent has been either:"]},{"k":"li","s":["exchanged at ‘Himbol’, the state foreign currency exchange"]},{"k":"li","s":["spent at an official hotel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you cannot account for foreign money you’ve spent, you may be delayed or face prosecution, leading to a severe fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["You are not allowed to take more than 1,000 Eritrean nafka out of Eritrea."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Eritrea","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Eritrea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Eritrea, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Military activity in the Red Sea area"]},{"k":"p","s":["Military activity is currently underway in response to attempts by Houthi militants to prevent movement of international shipping in the Red Sea. While the area of activity is limited to the Red Sea and Yemen, there is a possibility that Travel Advice for nearby countries could change at short notice. You should continue to monitor Travel Advice and follow any relevant instructions from local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Local security measures"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are periodically reports of conscription surges and mobilisation of reservists in Eritrea, connected to regional instability of the Horn of Africa. Security measures may be in place around Asmara and other regions of Eritrea. Get advice from your host, accommodation or travel operator."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tensions between Eritrea and Ethiopia are high. The security situation could change with little notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay away from areas that are close to security/military installations or activity. Security/military locations can change, so seek local advice where possible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Armed civilians"]},{"k":"p","s":["A large proportion of the population has access to arms under the government of Eritrea’s civilian militia programme. The British Embassy has no evidence these weapons increase the threat of violent crime."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals must apply in advance for a permit to travel outside Asmara’s surrounding province, Zoba Maekel, as well as to certain sites within the capital like the ‘tank graveyard’. There are checkpoints outside Asmara where officials will check your travel permit. Applications for permits are handled by the relevant ministry:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ministry of Trade and Industry for business travellers"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ministry of Tourism, Harnet Avenue, for tourists"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ministry of Foreign Affairs for diplomats"]},{"k":"p","s":["Applications may take several days to be processed and are not always successful."]},{"k":"p","s":["When applying, you must give details of the car you’ll be travelling in. There have been reports of authorities not allowing tourists to use public transport for travel outside of Asmara."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are living or working outside Asmara, you will also need a travel permit to leave your area of residence or work. Apply to the local region (‘zoba’) administration office."]},{"k":"p","s":["Restrictions on travel by foreign nationals apply equally to foreign diplomats. Staff from the British Embassy cannot always provide consular assistance in person to British nationals outside Asmara."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Though Asmara is a relatively safe city, there is a risk of street crime, especially at night. Women travellers can experience verbal and physical harassment by individuals or groups of men. To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not walk alone at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep phones, cameras and passports out of sight"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep valuables somewhere secure, such as in a hotel safe"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry ID. A copy of the photo page of your passport is enough. Keep the original and a second copy in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Internet and phone access"]},{"k":"p","s":["Internet access is highly restricted in Eritrea, mainly limited to hotels and a small number of internet cafes. There is no 3G in the country. The national telephone networks are often unreliable and may only work for limited periods each day outside Asmara and larger towns."]},{"k":"p","s":["International SIM cards do not work in Eritrea. You need a residence permit to buy a local SIM card and this can take several weeks. There have been unconfirmed reports that phone calls made on the Eritrean mobile network are recorded."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Photography"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photographing government buildings and military installations is illegal. Always ask if you want to take a photo in any area where security personnel are present. You need a permit to take photographs of the ‘tank graveyard’ in Asmara. You can apply for a permit at the Ministry of Tourism."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal. If convicted, you can get a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Eritrea, you will need a ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence. You cannot get an IDP outside the UK so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take both your IDP and UK driving license to the Ministry of Transportation and Communication and they will issue you with a driving permit."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road signage and safety barriers are scarce and road surfaces are uneven. Tight blind bends and steep drops are common. Street lighting is limited and may be affected by power cuts. Other drivers may drive without lights and some drive erratically or at speed. In many parts of the country, roads are difficult or impassable during the rainy season."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The runway at Asmara International Airport is occasionally damaged by weather conditions, particularly during the rainy season. If this happens, flights may be delayed or cancelled until the runway has been repaired, and travellers may experience significant disruption."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List (ASL)","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," lists all known airlines in Eritrea that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check whether your tour operator has concerns about airlines in Eritrea."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mariners should get permissions and entry visas before attempting to enter Eritrean waters. Vessels have been impounded and crew detained for entering Eritrean waters or landing in Eritrea, including islands belonging to Eritrea without permission."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Piracy risk"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Southern Red Sea area is a hotspot for maritime crime and security incidents."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is still a significant risk of ",["piracy in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],", where piracy has been reduced but not prevented. The threat assessment of the combined international naval counter-piracy forces is that sailing yachts should not enter the ",["designated high-risk area,","https://on-shore.mschoa.org/"]," due to the risk of hijacking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Eritrea. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Military activity in the Red Sea area"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of military activity is currently underway in response to attempts by Houthi militants to prevent movement of international shipping in the Red Sea. While the area of activity is limited to the Red Sea and Yemen, there is a possibility that the situation could change at short notice. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information"]},{"k":"h","s":["Eritrea-Djibouti border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 25km of Eritrea’s border with Djibouti."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2008 there was fighting between Djibouti and Eritrea after an incursion of Eritrean forces into the disputed Djibouti border region. The situation remains fragile."]},{"k":"h","s":["Eritrea-Ethiopia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 25km of Eritrea’s border with Ethiopia because of military activity on both sides of the border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Eritrea-Sudan border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 25km of Eritrea’s border with Sudan because of military activity on both sides of the border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Hanish Islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is highly unlikely that Eritrean authorities will issue permits for any vessels to visit the south-western Hanish Islands. These islands are very close to the conflict in Yemen. The authorities have previously detained mariners who landed without a permit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines near borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of landmines near Eritrea’s borders, particularly in the Eritrea-Ethiopia and Eritrea-Djibouti border areas. If you are in the border area against FCDO advice, do not leave the main paved highways by car or on foot."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 122244 and ask for an ambulance. Please note that the call handler may not speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccinations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the latest information on ",["vaccination recommendations and health risks in TravelHealthPro’s Eritrea guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/74/eritrea"]]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Eritrea. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a limited range of medicines available in Eritrea, and many of those are produced locally. If you’re taking prescription medication, make sure you have a supply for your stay plus a contingency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS has information on ",["whether you can take your medicine abroad","https://www.nhs.uk/common-health-questions/medicines/can-i-take-my-medicine-abroad/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare facilities in Eritrea"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are 3 public hospitals in Asmara. Public hospitals in other towns are often poorly equipped. In rural areas medical facilities are even more limited. If you’re travelling away from the large towns, carry a comprehensive medical pack with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Eritrea","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/doctors-and-medical-facilities-worldwide-list"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Eritrea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 122244"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 116"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 113"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Consular assistance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Consular support is severely limited in parts of Eritrea. Constraints on travel within Eritrea mean the British Embassy is often unable to deliver in-person consular assistance outside the greater Asmara area."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Eritrean authorities may not inform the British Embassy if a British national is in need of help. There have been instances where the Eritrean authorities have refused to give the Embassy consular access to detained foreign nationals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=eritrea"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=eritrea"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=eritrea"]," in Eritrea"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Eritrea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/eritrea-bereavement-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Eritrea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/eritrea-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]," such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/eritrea/british-embassy-asmara"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/eritrea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":18782,"change":"Removal of information about the temporary withdrawal of dependants of British Embassy staff from Eritrea ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/honduras":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"fdaf3c31bccb464bc38985061763f4d18c0cf0f5ef691720a073a7fc1b0d512a","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/honduras","bytes":60252,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Honduras travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-26T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-05T14:10:43+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/honduras/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Honduras current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Honduras set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Honduran Embassy in the UK","https://hondurasembassyuk.com/"]," (Spanish language website)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Honduras, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least 2 blank pages. Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["British citizens can visit Honduras for up to 90 days without a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["This visa exemption for British citizens took effect on 31 October 2026. Contact the ",["Honduran Embassy","https://hondurasembassyuk.com/"]," in the UK for further information on entry requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay the 90 days, you may have to pay a fine before leaving Honduras. Contact the Honduran National Institute of Migration for information on overstaying or extending your stay."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for or extending your stay"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer than 90 days, including to work, study or for business, you must meet the Honduran government’s entry requirements. Check what type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Honduran Embassy","https://hondurasembassyuk.com/"]," in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will get a 30-day visit entry stamp in your passport when you arrive. Make sure the border control officer puts a stamp in your passport otherwise you may get a fine. If your passport is missing a stamp, return to the immigration desk immediately, or go to the National Institute of Migration in Tegucigalpa as soon as possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply at an immigration office to extend your stay."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling through Honduras"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling through Honduras to another country (sometimes called ‘transiting’), you must follow Honduran entry requirements even if you do not pass through immigration. Contact the National Institute of Migration (Spanish language website) for information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling between Honduras, El Salvador, Guatemala and Nicaragua"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel between Honduras, Guatemala, Nicaragua and El Salvador for up to 90 days without a visa. Read the travel advice for:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["El Salvador","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/el-salvador/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Guatemala","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guatemala"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Nicaragua","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The 90-day period starts when you enter any of these countries and does not restart when you cross borders. You’ll have to go through immigration checks at borders. If you’re expelled from one of these countries, you’re also excluded from the other 3."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you wish to extend your stay, contact the National Institute of Migration (Spanish language website) in Honduras. If you overstay, you may get a fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travellers aged 20 and under"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter or exit Honduras, people aged 20 and under travelling alone or with only one parent or legal guardian must have a notarised letter in Spanish from the parents or guardians not travelling with them. Contact the ",["Honduran Embassy","https://hondurasembassyuk.com/"]," (Spanish language website), or if you’re in Honduras the nearest National Institute of Migration (Spanish language website), for information about what documents you need. Single parents will need additional documents."]},{"k":"h","s":["Airport tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an airport departure tax for international flights ranging from USD40 - USD55 (or the same amount in Honduran lempiras) depending on the airport. This is normally included in the cost of your ticket."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also a lower rate departure tax for domestic flights, again, normally included in the cost of your ticket."]},{"k":"h","s":["Land border fee"]},{"k":"p","s":["When you arrive at a land border, the immigration authorities may charge you a fee of 3 US dollars (in cash). Keep the receipt until you leave Honduras as you may be asked to present it and make sure you get a stamp in your passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need a yellow fever certificate for onward travel to some other countries, due to the risk of yellow fever in Honduras."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Honduras guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/101/honduras#Vaccine_recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Honduras. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must complete the Government of Honduras’ ",["customs declaration form","https://sisglobal.aduanas.gob.hn/Pech/#/plataforma/otra_gestiones/formularioDJRV"]," prior to entering or leaving the country. After completing the online form, you must present the QR code to the customs authorities, either on paper or electronically."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Honduras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Honduras, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests can happen anywhere in Honduras. Although normally peaceful, these can rapidly turn violent with a general breakdown in law and order, including looting. The police have frequently responded with tear gas and there have been deaths and injuries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although protests are normally restricted to the main cities (especially Tegucigalpa, San Pedro Sula and La Ceiba), the authorities can set up roadblocks anywhere at short notice and these cause significant travel disruptions. Your travel plans may be affected at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for foreigners to participate in political activities. If you take part in protests, you may be detained and deported. Avoid all demonstrations and protests and do not try to pass through blockades. Follow the advice of local authorities and your tour operator or airline and monitor local and social media."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Honduras has one of the highest violent crime rates in Latin America. Although most serious crime does not affect tourists, you could be caught up in incidents as they can happen anywhere and at any time, even in tourist areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Petty theft is a problem in cities and tourist areas, including the Bay Islands (Roatán, Utila, and Guanaja). Avoid walking around Tegucigalpa, San Pedro Sula, and other main towns and cities in mainland Honduras. Be particularly careful at bus stations, airports, isolated beaches, tourist sites and on public transport. Keep your valuables locked away in a safe if possible. Avoid displaying valuable items like jewellery, cameras, tablets, laptops, and mobile phones."]},{"k":"hs","s":["ATM crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["ATMs are available in the major towns. Check with your hotel which ATMs to use, especially in Roatán. It is safer to withdraw money from ATMs in shopping centres and to change money in hotels or banks. Check ATMs for evidence of tampering, although affected machines may not be easy to spot. Do not withdraw a lot of money at one time and avoid withdrawals at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["People have been killed and injured resisting criminals. It is useful to carry a small amount of money to hand out if you’re robbed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent attacks against vehicles"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been violent attacks on people in cars and buses. Using a reputable tour company for longer journeys may reduce the risks, consider alternatives to public transport (buses). For shorter distances, use radio-dispatched taxis or hotel taxis. It is generally safer to travel on main roads between major cities and tourist destinations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take precautions such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["locking vehicle doors"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping windows closed"]},{"k":"li","s":["not travelling after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["travelling in convoy"]},{"k":"li","s":["not picking up hitchhikers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care if you’re travelling alone. In remote areas it may be safer to travel with others or join a tour. Do not accept lifts from strangers or hitchhike."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been attacks on roads:"]},{"k":"li","s":["from Limones to La Union"]},{"k":"li","s":["from Olancho via Salama to Saba"]},{"k":"li","s":["from Gualaco to San Esteban"]},{"k":"li","s":["from La Esperanza to Gracias"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the Department of Santa Barbara"]},{"k":"li","s":["in and around Tela, La Ceiba, Trujillo and El Progreso"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Scammers often target foreign visitors and residents. The scams come in many forms and can cause great financial loss. Warn your friends and family to be sceptical if they’re asked to transfer funds to you in Honduras. Tell them to contact you to check that you’ve made this request."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID and travel documents"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry photo ID. Carry a copy of the photo and visa pages of your passport with you. Leave the original in a safe place."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you always have the documents for your hotel, car rental, tour or ticket reservations. Local authorities may stop you and ask for documents confirming your travel plans."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for drug trafficking (15 to 20 years in prison and a very large fine) and drug use (from 3 to 9 months in a rehabilitation centre). Honduran prisons are overcrowded and violent."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal. There are no laws guaranteeing freedom from discrimination on the grounds of sexual orientation. There is no recognition of same-sex marriage. People in the capital, Tegucigalpa, are largely tolerant of individuals’ personal lifestyles and accept small signs of affection between same-sex couples. There is a more conservative attitude outside the capital and showing affection in public is not recommended."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["US dollars are widely accepted for exchange and payment. It is difficult to exchange British pounds in Honduras."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving accidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a hyperbaric (recompression) chamber on Roatán and there are recompression facilities on the Bay Island of Utila. However, emergency medical facilities on the Bay Islands are extremely limited."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Honduras, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Honduras for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are involved in an accident, contact the police or the fire brigade (telephone: 911), stay with your vehicle and wait for the police to arrive. If you’re in a serious accident, you may be taken into custody regardless of responsibility. Seek legal help and inform the ",["British Embassy in Guatemala","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-honduras"],". Take full details of the other driver (who may not be insured), and do not rely solely on the vehicle’s number plate."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards in Honduras are generally poor. Avoid road travel at night. Many vehicles travel without lights, and animals often wander across roads causing accidents. You may need a 4-wheel drive vehicle if you are not travelling on main roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public buses are often poorly maintained, overcrowded and recklessly driven. Accidents are common and sometimes fatal. Luxury buses, operated by private companies, are usually better maintained."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some roads remain damaged by hurricanes that struck in 2020."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Airlines in Honduras can change their schedules at short notice. Before you travel, check with your airline or travel agent."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drought, forest fires and flash flooding are common in Honduras."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The hurricane season in Honduras normally runs from May to November. Landslides and flooding can affect roads throughout the country. Monitor local weather reports and check the warnings from the US National Hurricane Center. Follow the advice of local authorities, including any evacuation orders. See the Honduran national civil protection website ",["COPECO","https://copeco.gob.hn/"]," (Spanish language website)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Honduras. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"]," and tsunami."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Honduras. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/honduras"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/honduras/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Borders with Guatemala, El Salvador and Nicaragua"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed robbers have targeted travellers after they cross the Honduran border into El Salvador. It is often better to cross borders in the morning as they sometimes close in the early evening and remain closed at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are unmarked minefields in and around the border with Nicaragua. Avoid walking on unmarked paths or off main roads in these areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bay Islands and north coast"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Bay Islands are generally safer than mainland Honduras, but there have been several attacks by criminals on visitors, including on the ferries to and from mainland Honduras. If you are visiting Roatán, travel with a reputable guide. If you are driving a car or scooter, avoid side roads in remote areas, which can be poorly maintained and unsafe during night time hours."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care on beaches in the north coast towns after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of criminal attacks and carjackings in and around Tela, La Ceiba, Trujillo and El Progreso."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/101/honduras"]," for Honduras"]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Honduras","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/101/honduras#General_Information"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Honduras. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tap water is not generally safe to drink, but bottled water is cheap and widely available."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot use British-issued prescriptions in Honduras. To find a pharmacy (‘farmacia’) look for one of the big national chains such as Farmacias Siman, Farmacias Kielsa or Farmacia El Ahorro."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Honduras"]},{"k":"p","s":["State-funded hospitals are underfunded and medicines are in short supply. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation. Always carry evidence of your insurance. Use private clinics where possible, though these are only available in major towns."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Honduras","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilities-in-honduras"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Honduras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Honduras"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Honduras"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=honduras"]," in Honduras"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Honduras","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/death-pack-honduras"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Honduras","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/prisoners-pack-for-honduras"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"h","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/honduras/british-embassy-guatemala-city"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/honduras/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Honduras","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-honduras"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":18471,"change":"Updated information about visa requirements, including British citizens now being able to visit Honduras for up to 90 days without a visa ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iran":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-20T16:50Z","sha":"d754163cb9058758d9ca7746b148ff87949e710d293025ce5c01dba5174e2761","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/iran","bytes":82707,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Iran travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-18T16:30:59+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Iran"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Iran. If you are a British national already in Iran, either resident or visitor, carefully consider your presence there and the risks you take by staying."]},{"k":"p","s":["British and British-Iranian dual nationals are at significant risk of arrest, questioning or detention. Having a British passport or connections to the UK can be reason enough for the Iranian authorities to detain you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iran/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and military infrastructure. There remains a risk of further attacks across the region at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iran/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure"]},{"k":"h","s":["If you are in Iran"]},{"k":"p","s":["Air, sea and land routes are under the control of the Iranian authorities. Ports and borders may close at short notice. There is ongoing disruption to communications across Iran, with limitations on internet access."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US and Israel have struck infrastructure across Iran. There are reports that suggest ports, roads, railways, bridges, energy facilities, oil production sites, water systems, and airports have been affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals and British-Iranian dual nationals face a very high risk of arrest, detention and questioning."]},{"k":"p","s":["Holding a British passport or having perceived connections to the UK can be reason enough for the Iranian authorities to detain you."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are detained in Iran, you could face months or years of imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel by air"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot fly directly from Iran to the UK. A limited number of commercial airlines continue to operate international flights out of Iran. Iranian airspace may close at short notice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel by land"]},{"k":"p","s":["Iran’s borders with neighbouring countries may have restrictions for foreign travellers and may close at short notice. If you plan to depart Iran across a land border and consider it safe to do so, check the travel advice of the country you intend to enter before travelling to the border, including visa requirements. Entry requirements may change at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Entry to countries bordering Iran is not straightforward, and some countries will ask for additional paperwork for British passport holders. If you intend to leave overland you do so at your own risk. Should you require assistance, including with additional paperwork, ",["contact the FCDO","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/home"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Armenia-Iran border crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals do not need a visa for Armenia for stays of up to 180 days per year. Check our ",["travel advice for Armenia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/armenia"]," for the latest information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Azerbaijan-Iran border crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["To cross this border, FCDO must register your details with the Azerbaijani authorities in advance so that we can provide you with a registration code. This process can take several weeks. You will also require a visa to enter Azerbaijan. Read ",["travel advice for Azerbaijan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/azerbaijan"]," for the latest information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Turkey-Iran border crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["The border remains open visa-free for people travelling on UK or Iranian passports (for stays of up to 90 days). If you are a British national intending to cross the land border from Iran into Turkey, you must request facilitation from the British Embassy in Ankara ",["by contacting the FCDO","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/home"]," before travelling to the border. You must state which border point you intend to use and provide personal details (name, date of birth, details of travel document used to enter Turkey). Also indicate whether you are contacting from Iran or from the UK on behalf of a relative."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Turkish authorities advise that the Iranians have closed the crossing point at Esendere-Serow on the Iranian side to daily traders entering and exiting over the course of a day."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check our ",["travel advice for Turkey","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/turkey"]," for the latest information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Turkmenistan-Iran border crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["To cross this border, you require special permission from the Turkmenistan authorities in advance. This can be facilitated by the British Embassy in Ashgabat by ",["contacting the FCDO before you travel to the border","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/home"],". Without their prior approval, you will not be allowed to cross the border. You will also need a confirmed onward flight."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check our ",["travel advice for Turkmenistan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/turkmenistan"]," for the more information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Afghanistan border crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["The FCDO ",["travel advice for Afghanistan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan"]," advises against all travel to Afghanistan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Iraq border crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["The FCDO’s ",["travel advice for Iraq","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iraq"]," advises against all travel to Iraq."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pakistan border crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["The FCDO’s ",["travel advice for Pakistan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan"]," advises against all travel to Balochistan Province bordering Iran."]},{"k":"h","s":["Limited UK government support"]},{"k":"p","s":["UK government support is extremely limited in Iran. No face-to-face consular assistance will be possible in an emergency and the UK government will not be able to help you if you get into difficulty in Iran."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel to Iran against FCDO advice, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iran/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel against FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Iran’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Iran set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Iranian Embassy in the UK","https://uk.mfa.gov.ir/en"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You are at risk of arrest, detention and a death sentence if you travel to Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are at increased risk of questioning and detention by the Iranian authorities. See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iran/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to enter Iran against FCDO advice, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive. It’s not possible to apply for a British passport from Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Previous travel to Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your passport has stamps from Israel or other countries’ border crossing points with Israel, you may be refused entry to Iran."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Overseas British passport applications"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot apply for a British passport from Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["apply in a neighbouring country","https://www.gov.uk/overseas-passports"],". Choose from the list of countries and follow the application process for that country."]},{"k":"p","s":["For help with your passport application, ",["contact HM Passport Office","https://www.gov.uk/passport-advice-line"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Iranian dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Iran does not recognise dual nationality. If you are a dual national, the Iranian authorities will consider you to be an Iranian national. They are highly unlikely to accept any requests made by the UK government on your behalf."]},{"k":"p","s":["All Iranian nationals must enter and leave Iran using an Iranian passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also need to prove to the Iranian authorities that you have the right to enter the UK. You must be able to produce your British passport or a valid UK visa in your Iranian passport on request. You may face increased scrutiny, questioning or detention because of your connection to the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Media reports suggest Iran is willing to detain people who have been visiting relatives inside Iran. Having travelled to and from Iran previously without issue does not guarantee your safety. See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iran/safety-and-security"]," for more information about the risks British nationals face in Iran."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Being considered an Iranian national"]},{"k":"p","s":["Even if you do not consider yourself Iranian, the Iranian authorities may see you as an Iranian national. For example, if your father is Iranian, or if you’re married to an Iranian man."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Iran unless you hold an Iranian passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the expiry date of your visa before travelling. If you overstay your visa, you may have to stay in Iran until this is resolved and you may be detained."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling through an Iranian airport, check visa requirements with your airline and the ",["Iranian Embassy in the UK","https://london.mfa.ir/en"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel to Iran against FCDO advice, apply for a visa well in advance of your travel. The application process for an Iranian visa can be long and unpredictable."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to travel to Iran with a British passport, the Iranian Embassy has told FCDO you must either apply as part of an organised tour or have a sponsor in Iran to get a visa. Check with the ",["Iranian Embassy in the UK","https://london.mfa.ir/en"]," for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must be valid for at least 6 months from the date you submit your visa application."]},{"k":"p","s":["Women and girls aged 10 or over should wear a headscarf in their visa application photos."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some British nationals have had problems getting visas from private online visa agencies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Iran, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine if you’re coming from a polio-affected country"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Iran guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/107/iran#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods that you can take into or out of Iran. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pork products"]},{"k":"p","s":["Importing pork products is illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Children travelling without a male parent"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Iran, a female parent travelling with her children must have the father’s permission, usually verbal, to take them out of Iran. Iranian immigration authorities will usually assume you have permission unless the father has petitioned the court, or the court has ruled to prevent the children travelling. For more information, contact the ",["Iranian Embassy in the UK","https://uk.mfa.gov.ir/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kish Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kish Island, you must arrange your visit through an Iranian travel agency. The agency must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["inform the Iranian Ministry of Foreign Affairs about your visit at least 2 weeks before you travel"]},{"k":"li","s":["have received confirmation that a visa will be issued on arrival"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["nearest Iranian embassy or consulate","https://uk.mfa.gov.ir/en"]," can give you advice and a list of registered travel agents."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must also have a hotel reservation before you travel. Your guide must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["pass a copy of the hotel reservation confirmation to the immigration office at Kish Airport at least 48 hours before you arrive"]},{"k":"li","s":["meet you at the airport when you arrive"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers have occasionally been denied entry to Kish without explanation. If you’re denied entry, follow the advice of your airline or travel agent."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Iran"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of recent attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in January 2024, at least 84 people were killed and more than 200 wounded in suicide bombing attacks in Kerman, southern Iran, carried out by Islamic State Khorasan Province (ISKP)"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2023, one person was killed and 8 wounded in a terrorist attack at the Shah Cheragh mausoleum, a Shia holy site in Shiraz southern Iran"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2022, 15 people were killed in a shooting attack at the Shah Cheragh mausoleum, Shiraz, in an attack claimed by ISKP"]},{"k":"p","s":["Baluchistan separatist groups have targeted government buildings and infrastructure in the Sistan-Baluchistan region of Iran resulting in casualties."]},{"k":"h","s":["Leaving Iran in an emergency"]},{"k":"p","s":["In an emergency, for example if there is serious violence, unrest or a deterioration in the security situation, the UK government will not be able to evacuate you, provide face-to-face assistance or help you if you get into difficulty. In these situations, it may become more difficult to leave safely. If you are a British national already in Iran, either resident or visitor, carefully consider your presence there and the risks you take by staying."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should have a contingency plan to leave Iran in an emergency situation. Air, sea and land routes are under the control of the Iranian authorities. You should not assume that ports and borders will remain open if there is a crisis. If your contingency plan involves direct travel to the UK from Iran, you may need to prove to the Iranian authorities that you have the right to enter the UK. You must be able to produce your British passport or a valid UK visa in your Iranian passport on request. You cannot apply for a British passport from Iran."]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk of arrest, detention and a death sentence"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a very high risk of arrest, questioning and detention for British nationals and British-Iranian dual nationals. If the Iranian authorities accuse you of security related offences as a British national in Iran, there is a risk that you will be sentenced to death."]},{"k":"p","s":["Holding a British passport or having perceived connections to the UK can be reason enough for the Iranian authorities to detain you. If you are detained in Iran, you could face:"]},{"k":"li","s":["months or years of imprisonment"]},{"k":"li","s":["a fine, which in some cases can be a significant amount"]},{"k":"li","s":["imprisonment until any fines owed are paid"]},{"k":"li","s":["strict bail conditions, including a travel ban or your (or your family’s) assets being used as security"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals, including British-Iranian dual nationals, and other foreign nationals, have been unfairly detained in Iran. They are often made to serve long prison sentences. In 2023, Iran executed some foreign national detainees, including a British-Iranian national. The criminal justice process in these cases falls below international standards."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Consular, welfare and family access while in detention"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are detained in Iran, your case will be in the hands of the Iranian authorities, who have demonstrated a pattern of hostility towards the UK and its citizens. If you are a British-Iranian dual national, the UK government will not be notified of your detention, nor will we be given permission to see you. The Iranian authorities will control your access to your family during your detention. If you die in Iranian detention, the Iranian authorities will control the notification process. There is no guarantee the Iranian authorities will inform family members or the UK government."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Iranian authorities have accused people with links to the UK of inciting protests. If you are in or near a protest, you are at serious risk of arrest. Mass arrests, including of bystanders, happen often. It is difficult to predict where protests will take place, and they may turn violent. British nationals arrested in connection with protests may come under increased suspicion of espionage or working to undermine the Iranian authorities. This can increase the risk of lengthy detention, criminal charges or receiving the death penalty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may also come under suspicion if you are near sensitive sites, have contact with Iranians who are of interest to the authorities for any reason, or are taking photographs. The Iranian authorities have arrested foreign nationals for possessing photographic equipment near sensitive sites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even if you avoid protests and crowds, there is still a very high risk of arrest, questioning and detention in Iran."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Activities that put you at risk"]},{"k":"p","s":["Having a British passport or connections to the UK can be reason enough for the authorities to detain you. Some activities put you at even greater risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["You are at greater risk if you have ever been involved with civil society organisations, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["charities"]},{"k":"li","s":["labour unions"]},{"k":"li","s":["human rights groups"]},{"k":"li","s":["environmental groups"]},{"k":"li","s":["political groups"]},{"k":"p","s":["Or are involved in other activities such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["journalism, including blogging"]},{"k":"li","s":["social media related to politics, journalism or Iran, including creating, ‘liking’, or sharing content"]},{"k":"li","s":["economic and academic institutions and think tanks, especially UK-affiliated institutions or institutions conducting research in/on Iran"]},{"k":"li","s":["protest movements, including the ‘Woman, Life, Freedom’ movement"]},{"k":"p","s":["Or are involved with any person or organisation that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["is seen as opposing the Iran government, either based within Iran or elsewhere"]},{"k":"li","s":["works on UK national infrastructure"]},{"k":"li","s":["receives public funds from, or is considered linked to, the UK government or law enforcement"]},{"k":"li","s":["was previously arrested, questioned or detained in Iran"]},{"k":"li","s":["is seen as having defected from the Iranian regime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Or you have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["any current or historical links to the State of Israel or Israeli nationals or institutions"]},{"k":"li","s":["any current or historical links to the United States government or public administration"]},{"k":"p","s":["Having a British passport or connections to the UK will put you at increased risk of scrutiny during times of national unrest, following any terrorist incidents, or when there is an increase in tensions between Iran and the international community."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Border areas are highly sensitive. FCDO advises all British nationals already residing in Iran against all travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 100km of the Iran-Afghanistan border"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 10km of the entire Iran-Iraq border"]},{"k":"li","s":["to the provinces of Sistan and Baluchistan"]},{"k":"li","s":["to the area east of Bam and Jask, including Bam"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is risk of banditry in the area east of Bam, Jask, and Sistan and Baluchistan. This is the main route for drug traffickers from Afghanistan and Pakistan. The towns of Zahedan, Zabol and Mirjaveh are particularly insecure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some Iranian officials and media reports have falsely alleged a UK connection to anti-government groups in Khuzestan, Kurdish-majority regions, and Sistan and Baluchistan. If you travel to these areas against our advice, stick to the main routes to avoid accidentally entering restricted or military zones."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take sensible precautions to protect yourself from street crime and petty theft. Avoid carrying large amounts of money and keep your passport safe."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been some attacks and robberies targeted at foreign nationals and tourists, including attempted robberies by thieves posing as policemen, usually in civilian clothing. If you’re approached by anyone who claims to be a policeman, ask to see ID and request the presence of a uniformed officer or marked patrol car. Do not hand over documents or cash, or get into a vehicle."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and Methanol Poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Getting cash in Iran is extremely difficult. Non-Iranian debit and cash cards will not work in Iran. It’s usually not possible to change travellers cheques."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to change money on the street. You can exchange selected foreign currencies in some exchange offices, though you may have problems changing money. Euros and US dollars are more commonly accepted than British pounds."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out before travelling how you will get enough Iranian rials for your visit legally. If you cannot, you may need to reconsider your travel plans."]},{"k":"h","s":["Surrogacy and adoption"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting Iran to arrange an international surrogacy or adoption, consider the risks and challenges involved. Surrogacy is a complex, lengthy process. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you’re aware of the facts and well prepared before starting the process"]},{"k":"li","s":["get specialist legal advice on Iranian and UK laws before making any arrangements"]},{"k":"li","s":["read FCDO and Home Office ",["guidance on surrogacy overseas","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/surrogacy-overseas"]]},{"k":"li","s":["research clinics and hospitals thoroughly to make sure they are safe and reputable"]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy cannot get involved in surrogacy arrangements or recommend hospitals or clinics."]},{"k":"p","s":["Commissioning a surrogacy will not automatically mean that the child holds British citizenship. To bring your child born through surrogacy from Iran to the UK, you must ",["apply for a full British passport","https://www.gov.uk/overseas-passports"],". You need an Iranian birth certificate for this. It’s not possible to apply for a British passport from Iran."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, do not eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress codes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Islamic codes of behaviour and dress are strictly enforced. In public places women must cover their heads with a headscarf, wear trousers or a floor-length skirt, and a long-sleeved tunic or coat that reaches to mid-thigh or knee. Men should wear long trousers and long-sleeved shirts in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are extra dress requirements at religious sites. Women may be asked to put on a chador (a garment that covers the whole body except the face) before entering."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Iranian authorities have arrested, detained and in some cases committed serious acts of violence against women and girls for not properly following dress codes. Enforcement ‘crackdowns’ can lead to large-scale arrests across the country at any time."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Relationships between men and women"]},{"k":"p","s":["Adultery and sex outside marriage are illegal under Iranian law and carry the death penalty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Relationships between non-Muslim men and Muslim women are illegal, although few westerners have been prosecuted. If a Muslim woman is found in a relationship with a non-Muslim man, she may be sentenced to be whipped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unmarried partners and friends of the opposite sex travelling together should be extremely cautious. Sex outside marriage and same-sex relations are against the law in Iran, with the death penalty as the defined punishment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Iranian hotel managers could insist on seeing a marriage certificate before allowing couples to share a hotel room."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ relationships"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are illegal under Iranian law and can carry the death penalty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Female travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Women should take extra care, particularly when travelling alone or with friends of the opposite sex. Women face a range of issues, from enforced hijab wearing to harassment due to there being relatively few foreign women in Iran. Respect local customs and avoid isolated areas. See more ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Streaming service bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many western streaming services including Netflix and Prime are banned in Iran."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol ban"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import, sell, manufacture or drink alcohol in Iran. This is on religious grounds, with exceptions only for certain recognised Iranian religious minorities. Drinking alcohol in public is not allowed, with no exceptions. Penalties can be severe."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and electronic devices"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photography near military and other government installations is strictly prohibited. You can be detained and charged with breaking national security laws. Sensitive government buildings and facilities are often difficult to identify. Take extreme care when taking photographs in any area. The Iranian authorities have arrested foreign nationals for possessing photographic equipment near sensitive sites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Using a laptop or other electronic equipment in public places can be misinterpreted, especially if your device contains photographs. You may be arrested and detained on serious criminal charges, including espionage."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s better to ask before taking photographs of people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import, sell, manufacture or consume drugs in Iran. Penalties for importing and possessing drugs are severe and enforced. Many people convicted of drug offences, including foreign nationals, have been executed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry copies of your passport photo page and visa for identification. Make sure you have a copy of the emergency contact details."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Satellite phones and drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need permission from the Iranian authorities to import or use equipment like drones or satellite phones. Using them without permission is illegal and you could be arrested."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mobile phones, internet access and communications"]},{"k":"p","s":["Iranian authorities have blocked, significantly slowed or shut down landline, internet and mobile services without warning in the past. This can be nationwide or localised. This can affect communication and location services on smartphones and other devices. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not rely on mobile data, non-Iranian mobile apps or international calls for personal safety"]},{"k":"li","s":["always keep an alternative means of communication and navigation with you"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure friends and family know where you are"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Business travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Individuals involved in commercial disputes with Iranian companies risk being stopped from leaving the country until disputes are resolved."]},{"k":"p","s":["Representatives of British or western companies may receive particular attention. British businesspeople travelling to Iran against our advice should take steps to protect commercially sensitive information, including password protection of electronic devices and not carrying unnecessary information. Electronic devices may be screened by customs officials on arrival and departure."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["Overseas business risk in Iran","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-iran"]," for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive in Iran, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a ",["1968 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," when using a UK driving licence to drive in Iran. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Iran has a high rate of road accidents. Take great care when travelling by car or public transport and when crossing streets. If you’re involved in an accident, no matter how minor, do not leave the scene. Wait until the police arrive to write their report."]},{"k":"p","s":["Iranian authorities sometimes set up informal roadblocks both in cities and on main highways. These are often staffed by young and inexperienced officers. Always carry identification with you and avoid getting into disputes."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is not widely accepted for women to drive motorbikes on public roads and there is a risk of being arrested."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Motorcycle taxis should not be used as they have sometimes taken tourists to quiet locations and robbed them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pre-booked taxis are safer than taxis hailed from the street."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," (ASL) lists all known airlines in Iran that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many areas of the Caspian Sea, Persian Gulf and Gulf of Oman are very politically and militarily sensitive, with increased military activity including seizures and attempted seizures, boardings and harassment of maritime vessels."]},{"k":"p","s":["The waters around the islands of Abu Musa and the Tunbs in the southern Persian Gulf are particularly sensitive. British national mariners should not dock or sail into waters around these islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["When in the region, maintain a high state of awareness and be alert to local and regional tensions which may affect your route. Vessels may be at increased risk of maritime attack and harassment if they operate in the:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Gulf of Oman"]},{"k":"li","s":["Northern Arabian Sea"]},{"k":"li","s":["Persian Gulf"]},{"k":"li","s":["Strait of Hormuz"]},{"k":"p","s":["Iran has repeatedly attacked commercial vessels in nearby waters with military drones. One attack in 2021 resulted in the deaths of a British and a Romanian national. Vessels have also been seized and their crews detained in and around the Gulf of Oman and the Strait of Hormuz in recent years."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your vessel is hailed, provide the vessel name, flag state, and confirm they are exercising navigation rights and proceeding in accordance with international law, as reflected in the UNCLOS Convention. You should maintain high levels of awareness when you are operating in the area and report into ",["United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations (UKMTO)","https://www.ukmto.org/"],". Record footage of all incidents wherever possible."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many parts of Iran are at risk of earthquakes and tremors. These can be high magnitude, cause damage to infrastructure and put lives at risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some provinces can suffer from floods in spring, particularly:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Khuzestan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Golestan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lorestan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local news updates"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor advice from local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["take waterproofs, thermals, hiking boots and rations when driving and walking"]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 115 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Iran","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/107/iran#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you will face in Iran","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/107/iran"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Iran. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Iran"]},{"k":"p","s":["In general, medical facilities in Iran are reasonable in the major cities but poor in remote areas. Many health professionals speak some English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reported shortages of some basic medicines in Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national in Iran having medical or cosmetic treatment, you may not get adequate care in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Iran","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/iran-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Iran"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 115"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 125"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 110"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Iran"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Iran"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Iran"]," in Iran"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Iran","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/iran-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/arrested-or-detained-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/iran/british-embassy-tehran"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Or in an emergency you can also call FCDO: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK government will not be able to evacuate you, provide face-to-face assistance or help you if you get into difficulty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iran/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Iran","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-iran"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":34647,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/poland":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"bcb24ea51482849e9a822e0bd878b2091876ba6b0980a76fac1563b7d71ebd0e","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/poland","bytes":93462,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Poland travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-22T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-11T15:42:44+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorist attack in Kraków’s Main Market Square"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you were affected by the 7 November attack, or are concerned about someone who may have been involved, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact the Polish police on 112 if you have information relating to the attack"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact the British Embassy in Warsaw if you require consular assistance"]},{"k":"li","s":["read about UK ",["Support for victims and survivors of terrorism - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/support-for-victims-and-survivors-of-terrorism"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Ukraine-Poland border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Russian military strikes have taken place in Ukraine within 20km of the Polish border. Access to the border is restricted. See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/poland/safety-and-security#Russian-invasion-of-Ukraine"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/poland/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Poland set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact ",["Polish Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.pl/web/unitedkingdom/embassy-london"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Poland follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Polish dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British-Polish dual national, you must enter and exit Poland using a Polish passport or Polish national identity card. There are regular cases of Polish border guards allowing dual nationals to enter on their British passport, but refusing exit on the British passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Children born to Polish or British-Polish dual national parents in the UK are automatically granted Polish citizenship, regardless of the child’s place of birth. The requirement to exit Poland using Polish documentation will apply."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out ",["how to apply for a Polish passport before travelling to Poland","https://www.gov.pl/web/wielkabrytania/paszporty?page=1&size=10"]," (in Polish). Check with the ",["Polish Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.pl/web/unitedkingdom/embassy-london"]," if in doubt about your circumstances."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel ",["without a visa to the Schengen area,","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"]," which includes Poland, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Poland","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-poland-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Polish border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Polish government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Polish Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.pl/web/unitedkingdom/embassy-london"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Poland with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Poland","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-poland#passports-and-travel"]," and read the ",["Polish Border Guards guidance","https://www.strazgraniczna.pl/pl/aktualnosci/8885,Wielka-Brytania-poza-UE.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Land border crossings"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Poland from Ukraine"]},{"k":"p","s":["The main border crossing points to enter Poland from Ukraine are listed on the ",["Ukrainian government website","https://dpsu.gov.ua/en"],". Prepare for potential long delays at border crossings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access to within 15m of the Poland-Ukraine border is restricted. Observe this restriction at all times unless you’re at a designated border crossing point. Follow the instructions of Polish authorities if you are in this area."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have arrived in Poland from Ukraine and are in need of assistance, call +48 22 311 0000 or +44 1908 516 666 and select the option for ‘consular services for British nationals’. You can also send an enquiry using the ",["web contact form","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/poland/british-embassy-warsaw"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Poland from Belarus"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Belarus. Poland temporarily closed the Poland-Belarus border including rail crossings from 12 to 24 September 2025. The border is open but certain border checkpoints are closed. Border checkpoints may close or have additional restrictions imposed at short notice and other disruption is possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access to parts of the Polish border with Belarus is restricted. The regulations, which came into force on 13 June 2024 was extended on 6 September 2025 for another 90 days, prohibits access to the border in specific areas controlled by the Polish Border Guard posts at Narewka, Białowieża, Dubicze Cerkiewne and Czeremcha. In some areas, access is restricted to within 200m of the border and in others to within 2km. See precise ",["details of the restricted areas","https://isap.sejm.gov.pl/isap.nsf/DocDetails.xsp?id=WDU20250000738"]," (in Polish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should check the ",["Polish Border Guards guidance","https://www.strazgraniczna.pl/"]," (in Polish), observe these regulations at all times and follow the instructions of the Polish authorities if you are in these areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Other Polish borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 7 July 2025, Polish border guards will implement controls at the German and Lithuanian borders for entry into Poland. Border checkpoints may close or impose restrictions at short notice and other disruption is possible. Check the ",["Polish Border Guards guidance","https://www.strazgraniczna.pl/"]," (in Polish) and follow the instructions of the Polish authorities if you are in these areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border controls at Germany’s land borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are temporary border controls in place to travel into Germany. Check the ",["entry requirements for Germany","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into and out of Poland. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food and drink into Poland"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Poland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Poland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Poland cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Russian invasion of Ukraine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some Russian military strikes in Ukraine have hit within 20km of the Polish border."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, there was an explosion in Przewodów near the Ukrainian border killing 2 Polish nationals. For the latest information, see ",["Ukraine travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ukraine"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access to the land borders with Ukraine and Belarus are restricted. See ",["Entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/poland/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public demonstrations are common. Marches and gatherings are mostly peaceful and well-policed, but take extra care in crowded places. Demonstrations, marches and gatherings can attract violence. Monitor local media and follow the instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Racially-motivated attacks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most visitors do not experience any difficulties. Serious crime against foreigners is rare, but crimes do occur and in some cases attacks have been racially motivated."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to street crime and petty theft. Criminals view foreigners as easy targets. Keep valuables and cash out of sight, especially:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in crowded areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["in tourist spots"]},{"k":"li","s":["at main rail stations and on all train services and overnight sleeper trains"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking in isolated areas alone, especially at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care after withdrawing cash"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unofficial taxi drivers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Unofficial taxi drivers often overcharge. Passengers have been attacked, including sexual assaults, in unofficial taxis and cars booked using ride share apps. See further ",["advice from the Polish police","https://ksp.policja.gov.pl/pl/dzialania/aktualnosci/60915,Kampania-spoleczna-pt-Swiadomosc-Komendy-Stolecznej-Policji.html"]," (in Polish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not use unofficial taxis. Official taxis will:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have the name and telephone number of the taxi company on the door and top of the taxi"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a rate card on the window of the vehicle"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis with a crest but no company name are not official."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and alcohol"]},{"k":"p","s":["Victims of spiked drinks have been robbed in bars and clubs. Be careful about taking drinks from strangers or leaving your drink unattended."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check your bill carefully when buying drinks in bars and nightclubs. Alcohol can reduce your vigilance, making you less in control. Visitors have been overcharged when paying for drinks at the end of the night by debit or credit card."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry ID. A printed copy of the photo page of your passport is acceptable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dual Polish-British nationals will be treated as a Polish national if arrested or detained by the Polish authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Poland have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol in public places. The police can arrest you and you could get a fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are drunk in a public place, the police can take you to a clinic to be medically assessed. You must stay there until you are sober, including overnight, and pay for your stay."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal, but Polish law does not recognise same-sex marriages and civil partnerships."]},{"k":"p","s":["Small towns and rural areas can be less tolerant towards LGBT+ travellers. There are LGBT+friendly restaurants, clubs and bars in many towns and cities including Warsaw, Krakow, Wroclaw, Poznan, Gdansk and Sopot."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jaywalking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police can fine you if you are jaywalking – ignoring pedestrian crossings or signals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Photography and personal drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid taking photographs and flying personal drones near military or other security installations and any buildings or items of national infrastructure, including some border areas. You must comply with signs prohibiting photography and personal drone use and follow the ",["Polish Civil Aviation Authority’s rules","https://ulc.gov.pl/en/drones/general-information"]," to fly a personal drone."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Reflective clothing"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Walkers and cyclists","https://ec.europa.eu/transport/road_safety/going_abroad/poland/other_en.htm"]," must wear a reflective item at night in non built-up areas. The authorities may hold you responsible if you are involved in an accident and not wearing a reflective item. If police stop you without a reflective item, you could get a fine of 100 Polish zloty (around £20)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Validate your public transport ticket at the start of the journey. You will get a fine if inspectors find you travelling on an invalid or unvalidated ticket."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Poland, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Poland guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/poland/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Poland for up to 6 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["When driving, always bring your:"]},{"k":"li","s":["driving licence"]},{"k":"li","s":["ID"]},{"k":"li","s":["car registration document"]},{"k":"li","s":["insurance documents"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to show these if you are stopped by the police or if you cross non-Schengen borders. If you do not have them, the police may take your vehicle and charge fees."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Poland, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP. Most car rental companies will not allow you to take a hire car across the Poland-Ukraine border."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to drive for longer than 6 months, see ",["driving requirements for residents","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-poland#driving-in-poland"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roadworks are frequent, particularly in summer, as the road network is repaired and upgraded. The major roads are heavily used by transport vehicles as Poland is a major east-west transit route."]},{"k":"p","s":["Minor roads and even some main roads between major towns and cities can be narrow and poorly surfaced. Driving after dark on these roads is difficult."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tolls"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must pay road tolls on some stretches of motorways, expressways and national roads. See the ",["toll operator website","https://etoll.gov.pl/en/"]," for details."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air Travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["In September 2025, drone incursions caused the temporary closure of Poland’s airports."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may receive alerts on your mobile phone from the Polish government in the event of extreme weather, a natural disaster or other emergency. These are in Polish and English, and you should follow the authorities’ instructions. You can find out information about the ",["text message alert system here","https://alert.rcb.gov.pl/en/alert-rcb/"]," and about the ",["Government Centre for Security","https://www.gov.pl/web/rcb-en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Poland","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/180/poland#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Poland","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/180/poland#General_Information"],", including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Poland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public medical facilities in Poland are similar to those in the UK. Private medical facilities are less expensive than the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Poland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/poland-list-of-medical-facilities/poland-doctors"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Poland, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Poland","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-poland"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Poland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 999"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 998"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 997"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Poland"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Poland"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Poland"]," in Poland"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Poland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/poland-bereavement-pack-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Poland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/poland-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/poland/british-embassy-warsaw"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/poland/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Poland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-poland"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":21282,"change":"Updated information following the terrorist attack in Kraków, including advice for those affected (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/europes-rwanda-return-hub-raises-serious-human-rights-concerns-a-migration-researcher-explains-291697":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"11a37eeaeef8390960da6c9ca3952a5dffec4ff66f297b149a9b95c651966364","read":"https://theconversation.com/europes-rwanda-return-hub-raises-serious-human-rights-concerns-a-migration-researcher-explains-291697","bytes":179332,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Europe’s Rwanda return hub raises serious human rights concerns – a migration researcher explains","by":[{"n":"Ahlam Chemlali","r":"Migration Researcher and Co-Director for the Centre for Coercion and Accountability, Aalborg University"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T13:44:42Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["When I met Chadi, a young Tunisian man recently deported from Italy after crossing the Mediterranean by boat, he was already planning his next attempt: “They brought me here, but I’m not planning on staying.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["His story is worth keeping in mind given that five EU governments – Denmark, Germany, Austria, Greece and the Netherlands – have ",["announced","https://www.infomigrants.net/en/post/74775/five-eu-countries-announce-concrete-plans-for-rwanda-deportation-hub-scheme"]," that Rwanda will host Europe’s first “return hub”. This will be a ",["migrant","https://theconversation.com/topics/migration-412"]," deportation centre, where people whose asylum claims have been rejected, but who cannot yet be sent home, will be held or resettled. The first transfers are planned for 2027, starting with a pilot of around 100 people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Human rights organisations have warned against hubs in Rwanda – with Amnesty International calling them potential ",["“black holes”","https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/09/migrant-return-hubs-risk-becoming-human-rights-black-hole/"]," for human rights. Indeed, Rwanda is a troubling choice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Its president, Paul Kagame, was re-elected in 2024 with ",["99% of the vote","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/7/16/rwandas-kagame-on-track-for-fourth-presidential-term"],". UN experts say Rwanda exercises significant control over the ",["M23 rebels in neighbouring Congo","https://www.ecoi.net/en/file/local/2142213/n2611394.pdf"],", the brutal conflict’s leading perpetrators of sexual violence. While in 2023, the UK Supreme Court ruled Rwanda ",["unsafe for asylum seekers","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/uk-supreme-court-rules-rwanda-plan-for-asylum-seekers-is-unlawful/"],". So how will Europe guarantee the rights of people it sends there?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rwanda has also done this before. From 2013, ",["Israel sent Eritrean and Sudanese asylum seekers","https://theconversation.com/threat-of-expulsion-hangs-over-thousands-of-eritreans-who-sought-refuge-in-israel-and-the-us-87898"]," there under secret deals. Many ",["had their documents taken and were smuggled onward","https://foreignpolicy.com/2017/06/27/inside-israels-secret-program-to-get-rid-of-african_refugees_uganda_rwanda/"],", some all the way to the Mediterranean."]},{"k":"h","s":["The flawed thinking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Governments have said that return hubs will ",["break the smugglers’ business model","https://www.nbcnews.com/world/europe/5-european-countries-aim-send-rejected-asylum-seekers-center-rwanda-rcna609731"],". Research points the other way."]},{"k":"p","s":[["A major study","https://mixedmigration.org/about/events-media/new-data-shows-how-migration-policies-are-fueling-the-smuggling-business/"]," based on interviews with more than 80,000 migrants and 450 smugglers found that tougher borders without legal routes increase demand for smugglers. My own research shows that smugglers often work hand in hand with the very authorities Europe pays to stop them."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK government ",["has said","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/eu-states-immigration-return-hubs-rwanda"]," it will watch the scheme “with interest” and has not ruled out joining."]},{"k":"p","s":["When asked why France wasn’t part of the group of five, President ",["Emmanuel Macron said simply","https://www.euronews.com/my-europe/2026/06/19/not-our-europe-macron-and-sanchez-slam-ineffective-return-hubs-for-migrants"],": “I have never seen a return hub in a third country operate.” He’s right. Return hubs are sold as an innovation, but the logic behind them – outsourcing migration control to countries outside Europe – is not new."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s called externalisation and it has been part of European policy for three decades. In that time it has proved ineffective, expensive and corrosive to international law."]},{"k":"p","s":["As Europe’s leading intergovernmental human rights organisation, the Council of Europe, ",["has noted","https://www.coe.int/en/web/migration-and-refugees/-/commissioner-calls-on-european-states-to-refrain-from-actions-in-externalised-migration-policies-that-may-lead-to-human-rights-violations"],", it has also meant outsourcing border control to countries with a documented history of serious human rights violations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Human rights abuses"]},{"k":"p","s":["I’ve conducted ",["fieldwork","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/14650045.2023.2198125"]," across North and West Africa for more than a decade, particularly in ",["Tunisia","https://research.diis.dk/en/publications/living-and-dying-in-transit-violence-bodies-and-survival-in-the-t/"],", ",["Libya","https://www.dignity.dk/wp-content/uploads/publication-series-8.pdf"]," and ",["Mauritania","https://africasacountry.com/2026/09/what-europes-migration-deals-are-really-buying"],".I have interviewed hundreds of migrants, and following these deals and their consequences on the ground."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2023 the EU struck a €1 billion (£860 million) deal with Tunisia, the so-called ",["Team Europe deal","https://malta.representation.ec.europa.eu/news/european-union-and-tunisia-political-agreement-comprehensive-partnership-package-2023-07-17_en?prefLang=de"],". Most of the money was loans and budget support for Tunisia’s struggling economy, but at its core the deal was about ",["border control","https://www.euronews.com/2023/07/17/the-contentious-eu-tunisia-deal-is-finally-here-but-what-exactly-is-in-it"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since then, violence and arbitrary detention have increased in an already authoritarian and repressive country, where being a Black, undocumented migrant is ",["itself a risk","https://www.amnesty.org/en/documents/mde30/0180/2025/en/"],". The same template was rolled out to Mauritania and Egypt in 2024. When I was in Mauritania earlier this year, I saw the same ",["pattern repeating","https://africasacountry.com/2026/09/what-europes-migration-deals-are-really-buying"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Offshoring asylum has been tried before. Denmark first proposed a ",["Rwanda-style scheme","https://www.fmreview.org/externalisation/lembergpedersen-whyte-chemlali/"]," in 2021. The UK went further, signing one, before courts blocked it and Keir Starmer scrapped it in 2024, having ",["spent roughly £700 million","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/7/22/uk-planned-to-spend-10bn-pounds-on-rwanda-deportation-scheme-home-minister"]," to send four people to Rwanda, all voluntarily."]},{"k":"p","s":["Today’s hubs differ in one way: they are for people whose claims have already been rejected in Europe, not for processing claims abroad. But the concerns remain the same."]},{"k":"h","s":["Expensive and fragile"]},{"k":"p","s":["One country hosts a return hub: Albania, which struck a ",["2025 deal with Italy","https://gr.boell.org/en/2025/09/10/fast-track-asylum-return-hubs-italy-albania-deal-trial"]," to convert its Gjadër centre into exactly that. The centres have drawn heavy criticism from ",["Italian courts","https://www.globaldetentionproject.org/european-court-ruling-challenges-italy-albania-detention-deal-and-other-externalisation-plans"]," and ",["human rights organisations","https://www.rescue.org/press-release/italy-albania-deal-launches-irc-warns-grave-risks-people-move"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albania itself has signalled that the arrangement won’t survive past 2030, when it expects to join the EU. That is the crux of the matter: deals like this are not a stable foundation for long-term policy. They can unravel whenever the political weather changes in the partner country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rather than treating these experiences as a warning, the EU is doubling down. With a future hub in Rwanda, questions remain unanswered: who is responsible if someone’s rights are violated there, the EU country or the host? And once someone arrives, how do you stop them from leaving?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The many people on the move I have met over the years are rarely discouraged by being returned, pushed back, intercepted or deported. It only makes their journeys longer, more expensive and more dangerous. As Chadi told me: “They can return me as many times as they want, but I will keep trying.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["This article was commissioned as part of a partnership between ",["Videnskab.dk","https://videnskab.dk/"]," and The Conversation. Articles are also published in Danish."]}],"chars":5079},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"e858b1407bde44cfe29d67bf4b82f3e989675842a0bb8e9098b9c35bbae62a93","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/uganda","bytes":97092,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Uganda travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-06T10:16:14+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Uganda’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Uganda set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Ugandan High Commission in the UK","https://www.london.mofa.go.ug/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Uganda, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Uganda. Check ",["which visa best fits your needs","https://visas.immigration.go.ug/#/help/visa"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["apply for a Uganda visa online","https://visas.immigration.go.ug/#/apply"],". You will have to attach the required documents and certificates."]},{"k":"p","s":["The immigration authorities will email you a letter of authorisation including a barcode. Print out the letter to show on arrival. Border officials will issue your visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternatively, you can take the letter to a Ugandan embassy and they will issue the visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also ",["apply for an East African tourist visa online","https://www.immigration.go.ug/services/east-african-tourist-visa"],". This costs 100 US dollars and allows multiple entries into Kenya, Rwanda and Uganda over 90 days."]},{"k":"h","s":["Airport entry restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["If someone is coming to meet you at Entebbe International Airport, you will have to meet them outside the terminal building. Only passengers with tickets are allowed in the building."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Uganda guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/231/uganda#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some countries have ongoing heightened health screening for travellers from Uganda. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["On 27 May, the Ugandan National Task Force on Ebola Virus Disease ",["announced","https://x.com/MinofHealthUG/status/2057471796497035293"],", a closure of the Ugandan border with the Democratic Republic of Congo, with limited exceptions for authorised Ebola response, humanitarian and security personnel. See ",["Health page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda/health#ebola"]," for further information about precautionary measures at entry points."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel operator for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK’s Returning Workers Scheme has been activated, due to the outbreak of Ebola. Returning health and humanitarian workers should check the latest at ",["UK’s Returning Workers Scheme","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/ebola-returning-workers-scheme"]," before returning to the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be taken into and out of Uganda","https://ura.go.ug/en/frequently-asked-questions-for-goods-handled-at-entebbe-airport/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda//warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["regional risks advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Uganda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Uganda."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in major cities and places frequented by foreign nationals and tourists, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["diplomatic premises"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["restaurants and bars"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["major gatherings such as sporting or religious events"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["security installations such as police stations"]},{"k":"li","s":["national parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities. The Uganda Police Force regularly issues alerts, particularly around public holidays or religious events."]},{"k":"p","s":["Consider whether locations that you visit have effective security arrangements in place, like bag searches, physical security and guards. Avoid large gatherings of any kind in Uganda as these may be targets for an attack."]},{"k":"p","s":["Previous terrorist attacks and disrupted attacks in Uganda have targeted the security forces, places where football matches were being viewed, restaurants, buses, schools, churches, national parks and government buildings."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been a series of terrorist attacks in areas of western Uganda near to the border with the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), including in national parks. You should exercise particular caution in these areas and follow the advice of local authorities. Terrorist attacks have also occurred in other parts of the country, including Kampala."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in December 2023, 10 people were killed in an attack on a bar and a farm in Kyabandara, and a further 3 people in an attack in Nyabitusi, in Kamwenge district near to Kibale forest"]},{"k":"li","s":["in October 2023, 2 tourists and their driver were killed by terrorists in Queen Elizabeth National Park"]},{"k":"li","s":["in June 2023, 42 people were killed in an attack on a school in Mpondwe, Kasese District, western Uganda, close to the border with the DRC"]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Presidential and Parliamentary elections last took place in Uganda on 15 January 2026. The Presidential Inauguration Ceremony took place on 12 May 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["Elections and political events have led to protests and violence, including fatalities. There has also been disruption to the internet and social media."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political rallies, protests and violent demonstrations in Uganda:"]},{"k":"li","s":["can happen anywhere without warning"]},{"k":"li","s":["can cause loss of life and injury"]},{"k":"li","s":["are more likely around elections"]},{"k":"p","s":["The police have used tear gas, rubber bullets and live ammunition to disperse demonstrators. Avoid all demonstrations and rallies where possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Red and yellow are strongly associated with political parties in Uganda. Consider not wearing these colours around political events."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you get caught up in a political demonstration:"]},{"k":"li","s":["remain calm and try to move away from the area by the safest possible route"]},{"k":"li","s":["lock the doors and shut the windows if you’re in a vehicle"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay inside if you’re in your accommodation and you think leaving is threatening or unsafe"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you’re familiar with the security procedures at your accommodation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may target tourists who show signs of wealth."]},{"k":"p","s":["Organised crime groups operate in Uganda. However, criminal kidnaps and targeted armed assaults are unlikely to be directed at tourists."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can reduce the risk of being followed and pickpocketed or mugged by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not carrying large amounts of cash"]},{"k":"li","s":["using arranged transport to withdraw cash"]},{"k":"li","s":["using indoor ATMs"]},{"k":"li","s":["not wearing expensive-looking jewellery or watches"]},{"k":"li","s":["taking care of your passport"]},{"k":"li","s":["not walking after dark"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may steal from cars and taxis stopped in traffic. Keep car doors locked and windows shut when driving in towns. Do not leave luggage or valuables in parked vehicles. Do not resist if armed criminals stop you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals using motorbike taxis (‘boda-bodas’) have been mugged. Some of these incidents have involved violence and the use of weapons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Food and drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers have been drugged and robbed on public transport and in bars. Do not accept food and drink from strangers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Scammers may target foreign visitors and residents. Be wary of strangers who:"]},{"k":"li","s":["approach you or your accommodation"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact you by phone asking for personal information or financial help"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["National cleaning day"]},{"k":"p","s":["The final Saturday of each month, between 7 and 10 am, is a mandatory and nationwide cleaning day."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to Government of Uganda guidance, Ugandans are expected to clean homes, neighbourhoods, markets, schools, health facilities, places of worship, roads, drainage channels and other public spaces. Foreigners are not the intended participants but may be affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["During this time, all businesses must close and all non-essential movement of people and vehicles is prohibited. There are exemptions for tourists, international travellers, medical staff, state security actors and journalists. Patients seeking medical attention are allowed to travel to health facilities. Cross border traffic is also exempt."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ugandan police will enforce the travel restrictions. Anyone travelling under one of the exemptions may be required to identify themselves and explain their circumstances to police officers."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is unclear how widely the restrictions are enforced and what the restrictions mean for UK travellers, including for hotel and airport access. Contact your travel provider for more information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Officials may stop you and ask for ID. Always carry a copy of the photo page of your passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wearing military-style clothing"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for anyone, including children, to dress in military-style clothing. This includes clothing with marks, badges or symbols and accessories associated with the Ugandan military, camouflage clothing and red berets. The offence carries a maximum sentence of life imprisonment when convicted."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Helping children on Kampala’s streets"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal and punishable by a fine and a possible prison sentence to offer money, food or clothing to children living on the streets in Kampala."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["public places"]},{"k":"li","s":["workplaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["outdoors if you’re within 50 metres of a public building"]},{"k":"p","s":["Electronic cigarettes and shisha (water-pipe tobacco) are illegal. There are penalties including fines and prison sentences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drug penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for illegal drug possession and illegal drug trafficking are severe. The maximum sentence is 20 years for possession and life imprisonment for trafficking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is forbidden to take photos of military, official or diplomatic sites. This includes Owen Falls Dam at the source of the Nile near Jinja."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are taking photographs of people, ask their permission first."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Uganda."]},{"k":"p","s":["In May 2023, Uganda introduced the Anti-Homosexuality Act 2023. This act introduces long prison sentences, and the death penalty in some cases, for same-sex sexual activity. There are also severe penalties for promoting LGBT+ rights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sexual activity with someone of the same sex carries the punishment of life imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Offences classed as ’aggravated homosexuality’ carry a sentence up to the death penalty (though the death penalty has not been implemented for civilians in Uganda since 1999). ‘Aggravated homosexuality’ is defined as sexual activity with someone of the same sex who is:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a person aged 17 or under"]},{"k":"li","s":["a person aged 75 or above"]},{"k":"li","s":["a relative or someone under your care"]},{"k":"li","s":["disabled or suffering from mental health issues"]},{"k":"li","s":["a person who is unconscious or under the influence of medicine or other substances that impair their judgement"]},{"k":"li","s":["under duress or misrepresentation"]},{"k":"li","s":["threatened or intimidated"]},{"k":"p","s":["A person who has a previous conviction of homosexuality or related offences can be charged with aggravated homosexuality for subsequent offences."]},{"k":"p","s":["Promoting or supporting homosexuality carries up to a 20-year prison sentence. This includes, but is not limited to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["encouraging or persuading someone to perform a same-sex sexual act or anything that is an offence under the act"]},{"k":"li","s":["publishing, printing, broadcasting by any means, information that promotes or encourages homosexuality"]},{"k":"li","s":["providing financial or other support that encourages homosexuality or the normalisation of acts prohibited by the act"]},{"k":"p","s":["The law could affect those who are exercising their freedoms of expression, peaceful assembly and association, to show support for LGBT+ people and rights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anti-LGBT+ rhetoric by religious leaders, politicians, government officials and the local media can incite homophobia against the LGBT+ community."]},{"k":"p","s":["LGBT+ people or those who are perceived to be LGBT+ may be at greater risk of harassment, imprisonment, blackmail and violence from people who view the law as justification for attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade its parts without a licence. If you’re caught buying or trafficking such goods you might be prosecuted and get a prison sentence or a fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Uganda, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Uganda with a UK driving licence for up to 3 months. For a longer period, you must get a ",["Ugandan driving licence","https://udls.co.ug/get-a-new-driver-licence"]," or a ",["1949 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],". You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travelling by road can be hazardous, particularly outside the main cities. Driving standards are poor and the accident rate is high. At night, other road users may be driving without lights and livestock roam across the roads. Accidents regularly happen on the Jinja-Kampala and the Kampala-Masaka roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Speeding is illegal in Uganda and the police enforce speed limit laws. You could get a fine, a prison sentence or both if caught speeding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid travelling outside of the main towns after dark, except on the roads between Kampala and Entebbe International Airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your vehicle is in good condition and stocked with items you might need in case of a breakdown or other incidents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been serious accidents involving Ugandan long-distance bus services. These include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["buses between Kampala and other towns in Uganda"]},{"k":"li","s":["international services to Nairobi, Kigali and Dar es Salaam"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals have robbed overnight buses after posing as passengers or blocking the road."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid using:"]},{"k":"li","s":["matatus (minibus taxis following a particular route)"]},{"k":"li","s":["boda-bodas (motorbike taxis)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Matatus and boda-bodas are cheap, but they do not meet UK safety standards. They are generally in poor condition, badly driven and often do not have proper insurance. Accidents are common and can be fatal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Boat travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ferry accidents on Lake Albert and Lake Victoria have killed large numbers of passengers in recent years. Overloading of passengers and goods is often the cause."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a reputable ferry company"]},{"k":"li","s":["not get on a ferry if it appears overloaded or unseaworthy"]},{"k":"li","s":["learn the emergency procedures on board"]},{"k":"li","s":["note the location of life jackets and emergency exits"]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Localised flooding and landslides are common, particularly during the rainy seasons from March to May and October to November."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Uganda is in an earthquake zone. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Uganda. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kampala"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kampala is a busy capital, take the same precautions as you would in the UK. See ",["Safety and Security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda/safety-and-security"]," for general risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["In June 2025, two security operations took place in Kampala. On 3 June, there was an explosion near the Catholic Basilica in the Munyonyo area. On 22 June, security forces killed one person in a security operation in Kalerwe Market."]},{"k":"h","s":["Uganda-DRC border"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Western Uganda"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Allied Democratic Forces (ADF), a militant group with links to Daesh, may target tourists and foreign nationals near the border between Uganda and the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC). There have been several terrorist attacks in western Uganda, especially around the Bwera border crossing. See ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Uganda and the DRC conduct joint military action against the ADF near parts of the Ugandan border, in North Kivu and Ituri provinces of eastern DRC. Ugandan troops are present on both sides of the border as part of the operations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border crossing points could close at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also a risk of banditry and localised violence near the Uganda-DRC border. There were co-ordinated attacks by local armed men against police and army installations in Kasese and Bundibugyo in November 2025, resulting in multiple deaths including of one civilian. Local authorities deployed security forces to the areas and multiple suspects were arrested. While tourists and foreign nationals were not specifically targeted, the attacks were close to tourist areas. If you plan to visit these areas, you should remain vigilant, exercise caution, and follow the advice of local security agencies."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the DRC provinces that border Uganda. See ",["DRC travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["South-west Uganda"]},{"k":"p","s":["The provinces of DRC bordering south-west Uganda have a history of instability and violent conflict and this can flare up with little notice. FCDO advises against all travel to these DRC provinces. There is a potential for some spillover into Uganda. Take care when travelling in the area."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are periodic clashes between DRC government forces and armed groups in the DRC close to the Ugandan border. The M23 armed group controls the Bunagana and the Kitagoma-Buszana border crossings in Kisoro district on the DRC side of the border. If you are in this area, keep your security situation under constant review."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border crossing points have been temporarily suspended in the past following clashes, and could be closed again at short notice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["National parks near DRC and Rwanda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use reputable, registered tour operators and contact the ",["Ugandan Wildlife Authority (UWA)","https://ugandawildlife.org/"]," for up-to-date advice and information before you travel. Mgahinga Gorilla National Park and Bwindi Impenetrable Forest National Park are in the extreme south-west of Uganda near the borders with DRC and Rwanda. It’s routine practice for security personnel to accompany tourists on gorilla-tracking visits in this area."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some gorilla trekking operators cross into DRC. Avoid taking these tours. FCDO advises against all travel to the provinces of DRC that border Uganda, including Virunga National Park."]},{"k":"h","s":["Uganda-South Sudan border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be extra cautious near the Uganda-South Sudan border. FCDO advises against all travel to South Sudan. See ",["South Sudan travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-sudan"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["North-east Uganda"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an increased security presence in north-east Uganda in the Karamoja sub-region (districts of Kaabong, Kotido, Abim, Moroto and Nakapiripirit) due to cattle theft. Military and civilians have been killed during security operations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed raids to steal cattle and robberies related to cattle trading, some resulting in killings, have been reported in Karamoja. There have also been robberies that have resulted in multiple killings in districts that neighbour Karamoja in the Teso and Acholi sub-regions. The attackers do not usually target foreign nationals, but you should always:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay alert"]},{"k":"li","s":["be cautious"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid travel at night"]},{"k":"p","s":["Parts of the north-east are likely to experience flooding during the rainy seasons, from March to May and October to November. Monitor local media and only use suitably equipped 4-wheel-drive vehicles."]},{"k":"h","s":["Eastern Uganda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel to eastern Uganda is largely trouble-free, but during heavy rains there is a risk of landslides, particularly in Bulucheke sub-county in Bududa District near Mount Elgon National Park, a popular tourist destination."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical help at the scene of an accident is likely to be limited, particularly outside Kampala."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["recommended vaccines for Uganda","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/231/uganda#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Uganda","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/231/uganda#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ebola"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"li","s":["Marburg Virus Disease"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Uganda. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional Ebola outbreaks in Uganda. On 27 August 2026, the World Health Organisation declared the Uganda Ebola outbreak over. The outbreak in neighbouring DRC continues and the risk of transmission into Uganda remains. Government of Uganda is continuing to implement precautions to reduce this risk, particularly in response to reported Ebola cases in the region among individuals who transited Uganda. You may experience screening and other precautionary measures at entry points, including Entebbe Airport. See the Ministry of Health’s ",["Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs)","https://health.go.ug/download/ebola-sops-may-2026"]," for more details."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro has information on ",["Ebola Disease in Uganda","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/ebola-disease-in-drc-and-uganda"]," and ",["general information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheets/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],". Some countries have heightened health screening for travellers from Uganda. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Health Security Agency has ",["Ebola information for humanitarian or healthcare workers","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/ebola-virus-disease-clinical-management-and-guidance"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drinking water"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only use boiled or bottled water and avoid ice in drinks. Avoid eating food prepared by unlicensed vendors or if you are concerned about kitchen hygiene. See ",["food and water hygiene","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/44/food-and-water-hygiene"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are staying in Uganda for a long time, store basic provisions such as drinking water and non-perishable foods at your accommodation, in case of supply problems."]},{"k":"hs","s":["HIV and AIDS"]},{"k":"p","s":["UNAIDS estimate that around 1,400,000 adults aged 15 or over in Uganda are living with HIV. Read more about ",["precautions","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/29/hiv-and-aids"]," and ",["how to avoid exposure to HIV or AIDS","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/search?s=HIV&ge_srch="],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Uganda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in Uganda are limited, especially outside Kampala. Many popular tourist attractions have poor medical facilities. If you are seriously ill or have an accident, you may need an air ambulance. Make sure you have appropriate travel insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Uganda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/uganda-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Uganda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=uganda"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=uganda"]," in Uganda"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Uganda","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-uganda"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Uganda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/uganda-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/uganda/british-high-commission-kampala"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Uganda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-uganda"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":25753,"change":"Updated information about precautionary measures in response to the Ebola outbreak in the region (‘Health’ page)."}};
